ince you\u2019re not forming new chows from hand, it\u2019s acceptable.\n\nBut critically: **you cannot Chi or Peng**, only Play. So you must choose the least harmful discard.\n\nFinal consideration:\n- B4: Was just played by you earlier? Yes \u2014 \u201cPlay B4\u201d in history. Already played once, so likely safe.\n- F3: You\u2019ve played it before (\u201cPlay F3\u201d), and others have too \u2014 very likely safe.\n- B7: Played by multiple players, including yourself \u2014 probably safe.\n- J2: Never discarded by you yet. First discard of J2 now \u2014 could signal holding a pair.\n\nThus, **discarding J2 now reveals your pair**, which is disadvantageous. Better to discard **F3**, which has already been seen, minimizing information leakage.\n\nMoreover, F3 is a wind tile (West), not your seat wind (South), and no one has Peng\u2019d it. It\u2019s completely safe.\n\nTherefore, **Play F3** is the best choice: it removes a useless honor tile that cannot contribute to any further meld in your hand, avoids breaking your J2 pair prematurely, and maintains safety.\n\nAnswer: Play F3"}
